{"tool_name":"rnaclust","contents":["biocontainers","bioconda","oeb","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"rnaclust","version":"1.3","home":"http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/~kristin/Software/RNAclust/","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"A tool for clustering of RNAs based on their secondary structures using LocARNA","identifiers":["biotools:RNAclust"],"description":"RNAclust is a perl script summarizing all the single steps required for\nclustering of structured RNA motifs, i.e. identifying groups of RNA\nsequences sharing a secondary structure motif. It requires as input a\nmultiple FASTA file. In the first step for each input sequence the base\npair probability matrix of its secondary structure distribution is\ncalculated (using RNAfold from the Vienna RNA package). Secondly, for\neach pair of base pair probability matrices a sequence-structure alignment\nis calculated using LocARNA. Lastly, a hierarchical cluster-tree (in\nNEWICK format) is derived by WPGMA clustering of the pairwise alignment\ndistances and the optimal number of clusters is calculated from the tree.\n","license_file":"COPYING","build":{"number":1},"requirements":{"build":["make",null],"host":["viennarna","locarna"],"run":["locarna","viennarna","perl"]},"source_url":"http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/~kristin/Software/RNAclust/RNAclust-1.3.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["RNAclust.pl --help | grep RNAclust.pl"]},"recipe_maintainers":["pvanheus"]},"biocontainers":{"name":"rnaclust","identifiers":["biotools:RNAclust"],"license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"A tool for clustering of RNAs based on their secondary structures using LocARNA","home_url":"http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/~kristin/Software/RNAclust/","keywords":["Sequences","Probability","RNA","Clustering"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"rnaclust","home":"http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/~kristin/Software/RNAclust/","summary":"It requires as input a multiple FASTA file. In the first step for each input sequence the base pair probability matrix of its secondary structure distribution is calculated. Secondly, for each pair of base pair probability matrices a sequence-structure alignment is calculated. Lastly, a hierarchical cluster-tree is derived by WPGMA clustering of the pairwise alignment distances and the optimal number of clusters is calculated from the tree.","addition_date":"2017-12-18T00:11:51Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-10T12:58:59Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"version":["1.3"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:rnaclust","credit":[{"typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"],"url":"http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/~kristin/"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de/~kristin/Software/RNAclust/manual.pdf"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Pairwise alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0491"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Sequence-structure alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0302"}]},{"operation":[{"term":"Structure alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0295"}]}],"name":"RNAclust","operating_system":["Linux"],"owner":"mbs_import","topic":[{"term":"Probability","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_2269"},{"term":"RNA","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0099"},{"term":"Sequences","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}],"validated":1},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:rnaclust:1.3/cmd/www.bioinf.uni-leipzig.de","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":true}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":0,"citations":[],"ref_count":0,"refs":[]}]}],"summary":{"description":true},"website":{"bioschemas":false,"copyright":false,"https":true,